            "name": "Danny Weinberg",
            "email": "danny.weinberg@discordapp.com",
            "date": "2019-05-20T17:26:42Z"
          },
          "message": "Allow running an iOS application with a custom bundle_name\n\nCurrently if you have a different `bundle_name` https://github.com/bazelbuild/rules_apple/blob/5b03711941f1201bae28d4e6ac8040dd7d1c7317/apple/internal/templates/ios_sim.template.sh#L164 will fail since it will be looking for the `ios_application`'s `name`, not `bundle_name`. This matches what is done below in `_register_macos_executable` and uses `bundling_support.bundle_name` to get the correct `.app` name.",
          "tree": {
            "sha": "3160155ebe1ec5fe4f53b7fde405c5dd8f6e1b01",
